 R←Test_StormGuard_003(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;parms;counts;html;i
⍝ `[TRAP]StormResetAfter`: an error that has not occurred for that many hours starts again at 1.
⍝ 0.0014 hours is about 5 seconds: long enough for three crashes in a row even with code coverage,
⍝ short enough for the test case not to wait for long.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 parms←∆StormGuardParms'Test_StormGuard_003'(,⊂'StormResetAfter = 0.0014')
 →T.PassesIf 0.0014=parms.stormResetAfter

 counts←html←⍬
 :For i :In ⍳3
     html,←parms ∆ProvokeCrash 501
     counts,←parms.stormCount
 :EndFor
 →T.PassesIf counts≡1 2 3
 →T.PassesIf html≡1 2 2                         ⍝ The 3rd occurrence is held back

 ⎕DL 6.5                                        ⍝ Longer than `StormResetAfter`
 html←parms ∆ProvokeCrash 501
 →T.PassesIf 1=parms.stormCount                 ⍝ Starts afresh ...
 →T.PassesIf 3=html                             ⍝ ... and gets the full treatment again

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
